---@class cloudflare.containers.ScheduledApplicationHealth
---@field errors cloudflare.containers.ContainerApplicationHealthErrorList
---@field instances cloudflare.containers.ScheduledApplicationHealthInstances Shows a count of application instance states.
---@field summary? cloudflare.containers.ScheduledApplicationHealthSummary|distilled.Null High-level health assessment. Only populated for "new_instances" strategy. Based on a sample of target-version instances rather than a full count.

---@class cloudflare.containers.ScheduledApplicationHealthInstances
---@field active number Number of instances whose runtime reports the container as running (container_status = "running"). This is a subset of the placements that remain up: an instance that is already bound to a Durable Object and serving traffic is counted under "assigned" until its container_status catches up to "running", so container_status can briefly lag Durable Object attachment under churn. To estimate running, Durable-Object-bound instances, sum "active" + "assigned" rather than reading "active" alone.
---@field assigned number Number of instances bound to a Durable Object with a running placement whose container_status remains behind "running". These count as live, serving instances; "active" + "assigned" approximates the running, Durable-Object-bound count.

---@alias cloudflare.containers.ScheduledApplicationHealthSummary "healthy"|"degraded"|"unhealthy"|"pending"

